docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:450:> **Who is not eligible for gastric bypass?** For Medicare-funded bariatric surgery, the usual wording is BMI 40 or above, or BMI 35–39.9 with a major obesity-related condition — always subject to individual clinical assessment. A BMI below these thresholds does not meet the stated MBS criteria; surgery may also be unsuitable if health risks, anatomy or the ability to follow long-term nutrition and follow-up need further assessment.
