content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:202:> Loose skin is common after significant weight loss. How much loose skin your weight loss results in depends on your age, your genetics, your skin elasticity, and of course, how much weight you lose. Exercise, particularly resistance training, can help with body composition during your weight loss phase. You might look into plastic surgery for loose skin (‘body contouring’ and ‘skin removal’) as an option down the track, though bear in mind it is not covered by the same funding pathways.
