content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:97:> 1. Initial enquiry and GP referral: most patients start with a GP referral, which can help with Medicare and private health requirements; if you contact OSWA directly, the team can guide you on what is needed. 2. Consultation with your surgeon: your surgeon reviews your history, goals and health conditions, then explains which surgical or non-surgical pathways may be appropriate. 3. Wider team assessment: this may include physician, dietitian and exercise physiology input. 4. Pre-surgery preparation: you receive procedure-specific preparation advice, including any pre-operative diet. 5. Procedure day: surgery is usually laparoscopic, with hospital stay and recovery guidance tailored to the procedure. 6. Long-term aftercare: follow-up, nutrition monitoring and habit support continue after surgery.
