   143	## Tone and compliance notes
   144	- Medical advertising: no guarantees, use phrases like "clinical averages", "results vary", "your clinician will advise", "many people experience"
   145	- AHPRA/TGA: no testimonials, no before/after claims, no guaranteed outcomes
   146	- MBS surgical threshold: state BMI 40+, or BMI 35–39.9 with a major co-morbidity as assessment guidance; BMI below 35 does not meet that MBS threshold. Do not present a lower-BMI statement as surgical eligibility.
   147	- GLP-1/medical-weight-management advertising policy is pending: use active-ingredient/class names only (semaglutide, liraglutide or GLP-1), never brand names, and verify the final TGA/legal position before publication
   148	- Voice: plain-language, empathetic, direct; avoid hype; this page is the broadest entry point and the reader may be at their most uncertain and guarded
   149	- Reader: a Perth adult at the beginning of their research, possibly BMI 27–35, may not know the word "bariatric", may feel shame or exhaustion — the page must normalise the conversation before it can sell it
   150	- This page should do the most to establish "obesity as a medical condition, not a willpower failure" — that framing is the emotional foundation the rest of the site is built on
   151	- Do not over-index on surgery; the medical management pathway is genuinely presented as an equal option on this page
