content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:182:> Gastric bypass surgery cost in Australia varies depending on your level of private health insurance cover, your surgeon and anaesthetist fees, hospital and theatre charges, and any out-of-pocket gap that applies to your situation. [Medicare item numbers 31572 and 31581](https://www9.health.gov.au/mbs/search.cfm?q=gastric+bypass&Submit=&sopt=S) attract a rebate when eligibility criteria are met, and private health insurance (typically a gold-tier or equivalent policy) covers the hospital and theatre component. Your surgeon's fee for a primary laparoscopic gastric bypass is $6,000 for both insured and uninsured patients, rising to $[X,XXX] for a complex case. For those without private health cover, or where out-of-pocket costs are a concern, superannuation may be accessible as a funding option in certain circumstances, including life-threatening conditions, certain psychiatric conditions, and the management of chronic pain. Financing options such as Zip and TLC are also available for eligible patients. A full breakdown of costs, funding pathways, and pre-surgical clinical fees can be found here.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:328:> **Can gastric bypass be covered by Medicare?** For Roux-en-Y gastric bypass, MBS item 31572 may apply when the relevant criteria are met, but Medicare does not usually cover every cost. Your surgeon can confirm whether an MBS item applies; your private health fund can confirm hospital-cover requirements, waiting periods and policy exclusions.
