content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-48-
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-49-### Content Gap Opportunity
--
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-51-1. **Cost transparency** — PAA shows explicit demand for "How much does gastric bypass cost in Perth?" and "Can gastric bypass be covered by Medicare?" — most competitor pages dodge cost. The brief's transparent itemised-estimate plus measured explanation of how Medicare and private health cover may apply directly fills this gap.
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-52-2. **Bypass vs sleeve comparison** — "gastric sleeve vs bypass" / "gastric bypass vs sleeve" carry strong AU volume (350+250) at near-zero difficulty, yet competitor bypass pages rarely tackle the comparison honestly. The brief's bypass-vs-sleeve note should explain procedure-specific trade-offs, including potential diabetes or reflux considerations, without implying a universal advantage.
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-53-3. **Type 2 diabetes outcomes** — No top result leads with type 2 diabetes outcomes despite this being a clinically relevant evidence-based angle for the bypass. Owning the "bypass for type 2 diabetes in Perth" angle is open, provided all outcomes are qualified and individualised.
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md:54:4. **Plain-language clinical clarity + named surgeons** — AHPRA rules block competitors from using before/after and testimonials, so the page must win on plain-language clinical clarity and named, credentialled surgeons (Dr Chandraratna, Dr Watson) operating at the same DR-70 SJOG Murdoch facility that already ranks.
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md:55:5. **Long-tail FAQ capture** — Recovery-time and "what you can never eat again" queries have meaningful volume and low KD — weave into FAQ for long-tail capture.
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-56-
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-57-### Recommended Word Count
content-briefs/gastric-bypass-perth.md-58-1,200–1,500 words (matches brief; top SERP competitors are clinic procedure pages running ~1,000–1,800w — depth on bypass-vs-sleeve, cost transparency, and diabetes outcomes is the differentiator, not raw length).
--
