docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md:242:> A gastric bypass is one of the most effective bariatric procedures available, but results depend on a combination of surgery and sustained lifestyle change. If weight loss is slower than expected or regain occurs over time, the first step is reviewing diet, habits, and follow-up care with your team. Further surgical options may be considered in some cases. Your surgeon and dietitian are there to support you through challenges, not just the initial recovery.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md-243->
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/gastric-bypass-perth.md-244-> Gastric bypass can be an effective bariatric procedure for suitable patients, but results depend on surgery, follow-up care, nutrition, activity and long-term behaviour change. If weight loss is slower than expected or regain occurs, your team can review your diet, symptoms and follow-up plan; further assessment or revision surgery may be considered in selected cases.
