content-reviews/am-i-eligible.md:273:> **1. My BMI is around 30; am I too low for weight loss surgery?** A BMI of 30-34 does not meet the MBS threshold for these items. Your surgeon can assess your wider clinical picture and discuss non-surgical medical weight management or dietitian-led care where appropriate; an individual assessment is still required.
content-reviews/am-i-eligible.md:323:> **7. What if I find out surgery is not right for me?** You will not leave without options. If surgery is not the right fit — due to timing, preference, or for clinical reasons — we can discuss medical weight management pathways including GLP-1 medications and dietitian-led programs. Some patients start there and revisit surgery later; others find it is sufficient on its own. The goal is the right outcome for you, whatever form that takes.
content-reviews/am-i-eligible.md:327:> **7. What if I find out surgery is not right for me?** Some people are not suitable for surgery straight away, or may not be suitable at all — suitability depends on an individual clinical-risk and aftercare assessment that your surgeon will explain. If surgery is not the right fit, non-surgical options can be discussed where clinically appropriate.
