845-+#### Paste-ready FAQ replacement
846-+
847-+> **7. What if I find out surgery is not right for me?** You will not leave without options. If surgery is not the right fit — due to timing, preference, or for clinical reasons — we can discuss medical weight management pathways including GLP-1 medications and dietitian-led programs. Some patients start there and revisit surgery later; others find it is sufficient on its own. The goal is the right outcome for you, whatever form that takes.
848-+
--
852-+>
853-+> **8. How much does weight loss surgery cost in Perth?** Costs vary by procedure, hospital, surgeon, anaesthetist, tests, private-health cover, excess, waiting periods and individual circumstances. Any applicable range or estimate is discussed at consultation, with an itemised breakdown before you decide.
854-+>
855-+> **9. Does Medicare cover weight loss surgery?** Medicare benefits may apply when the relevant MBS item, clinical and referral requirements are met, but Medicare does not cover every cost and no rebate should be assumed. The applicable item depends on the procedure—31575 is sleeve gastrectomy, 31572 is Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and 31581 is BPD/duodenal switch—so your surgeon and insurer should confirm what applies.
856-+>
857:+> **10. What is the 30/30 eating rule after bariatric surgery?** The 30/30 rule is an eating habit often recommended after bariatric surgery: take around 30 minutes to eat each meal, and avoid drinking fluids for 30 minutes either side of eating. Your dietitian will confirm the exact protocol the practice recommends for you. [30/30 protocol to be confirmed with the practice before publication]
858-+>
859-+> **11. What can happen over 10 years after weight loss surgery?** Long-term experiences vary. Some people maintain changes, while others regain weight, develop nutritional issues or need further treatment; ongoing medical, dietary and supplement follow-up may remain important. Your surgeon can discuss the evidence and what your health and follow-up plan may mean for you, but no single 10-year outcome can be promised.
