   241	>
   242	> A gastric bypass is one of the most effective bariatric procedures available, but results depend on a combination of surgery and sustained lifestyle change. If weight loss is slower than expected or regain occurs over time, the first step is reviewing diet, habits, and follow-up care with your team. Further surgical options may be considered in some cases. Your surgeon and dietitian are there to support you through challenges, not just the initial recovery.
